# tools/s/seed_link_witness.rish -- a link in a shipped document lands in the shipped tree.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. This tree publishes two ways from one set of files. The maintainer's field
# carries every room; the public seed is an ALLOWLIST projection named path by path in
# template-manifest.kyri. One README serves both. So a link that resolves perfectly in the field
# -- `gratitude/Rust.md`, `construction/ITINERARY.md` -- resolves NOWHERE for a reader who arrives at the
# seed, because the seed never carried that room.
#
# tools/t/tracked_link_witness.rish asks "is this in the repository." That is the right question
# for the field and the wrong one for the seed, which is a different repository with fewer rooms.
# Measured 20260823, before this rung: the front door alone shipped nineteen links into rooms the
# seed does not carry, and 867 stood across every living shipped document. No guard read it.
#
# THE REPAIR THIS ASKS FOR. A withheld room is NAMED IN PROSE rather than linked. The front door
# now describes the session logs, the operator card, the reading library, and the personal study
# room in plain sentences with nothing to click -- so the page is legible in both repositories
# and honest in each, rather than correct in one and broken in the other.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal.
#   Every relative link in a front-door document lands on a path the seed also ships. EIGHT
#   documents stand in that set from 20260916, named rather than discovered, so a new root file
#   cannot join it by accident and red on work it never agreed to cover.
#   Thirty-three behaviors on throwaway repositories, each with its own small manifest: the
#   agreeing tree free and reading zero, the regression refused, counted, and named, an unshipped
#   document free, a shipped non-front-door document counted as a ratchet rather than gated,
#   dated testimony free and uncounted, external and anchor links free and uncounted, a
#   second-step door refused and named, the roster's own size counted, the print cap holding at
#   five and --list naming every site, an unknown argument refused, and the ceiling proven from
#   both sides by planting exactly it and then one more -- no flag, no override. A second pen
#   carries the carried-room clause: its manifest allows one FILE under `deep/inner/` and never
#   a room, so the same tree holds a room the projection makes and a room no allow row reaches.
#   The own-room links are planted one past the ceiling, so a reading that counted them would
#   refuse, and the clause is proven a fifth time by being struck out of a copy of the scan.
#
# THE ROOM THE PROJECTION MAKES. `inseed()` walked UPWARD from a link target looking for an
# allowed ancestor, which is the right question about a FILE and the wrong one about a ROOM. The
# manifest allows `context/` twenty-one named pages and never the directory, so the projection
# creates `context/` to hold them -- step 6 of sow_project.sh derives every destination room
# from the kept list -- while the walk answered that the room was not there. On `20260917` the
# front door `context/README.md` began naming its own rooms with a `[./](./)` link and the
# ratchet crossed its ceiling at 821 on a link that opens perfectly in both repositories. The
# clause below the walk reads the allow rows' own ancestors: 821 to 820, exactly one site, no
# page edited and no ceiling moved.
#
# THE ROSTER WIDENED, AND THE READING THAT ASKED FOR IT. Run with the scan's five-line print cap
# lifted, the ratchet named 847 sites, and 27 of them stood on MAP.md, ORGANIZING.md, SOURCE.md
# and docs-geode/README.md -- the four doors the gated README.md links directly. The promise held
# for one page and the hand passed through at step two. All 27 were repaired the way this rung
# prescribes, the four doors joined the gate, and the ceiling fell 848 to 820.
#
# THE CEILING IS SPELLED ONCE. The control reads it out of the scan's own `ceiling=` line rather
# than carrying a copy, so a lowering reaches both readers at once. It was spelled twice until
# 20260916, which is the drift the ASCII-document family booked one instrument over.
#
# TESTIMONY IS ALSO A DIRECTORY SHAPE, NOT ONLY A BASENAME. On 20260926 the ratchet stood at 908,
# 528 over its own ceiling, and 509 of those sites lived under external-research/yonder/ -- retired
# countdown-prefix research notes (`9911_mem_concat.md`) predating the one-clock naming law, which
# never carry the stamp the elder testimony check reads. They are testimony all the same: a closed
# stack, the exact directory shape ascii_document_scan.sh and read-scope.md already read past. The
# reading now excludes any path carrying date/, archive/, or yonder/ as a directory component,
# whatever its basename, and the ratchet fell 908 to 380, ceiling lowered to match.
#
# WHAT IS REPORTED RATHER THAN GATED. The same reading across every other living shipped
# document, under a ceiling that only ever falls. The repair is a rewrite per document rather
# than a repoint, so it falls on touch instead of in one sweep that would bury the enforced zero.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN. That a link points at the RIGHT file -- tracked_link and living_docs_lint
# own resolution in the field. This rung asks only whether a link survives the projection.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/s/seed_link_witness.rish

say "seed-link: Language EN -- one page serves two repositories, and a promise kept in only one of them is half a promise."
say "seed-link: Style Radiant -- the tree names a withheld room in prose rather than pointing at a door that is not there."
say "seed-link: Lens TAME -- safety first: the seed is the face a stranger meets, and a broken front door is what they meet first."

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/s/seed_link_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "seed-link: a shipped document links into a room the seed does not carry -- read the scan's own lines"
assert scan.out contains "front_door_links_outside_seed=0" else "seed-link: every front-door link must land on a path the seed ships"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "seed-link: the scan must balance before it is believed"
say "field GREEN -- the front door reads whole in the field and in the seed alike"

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/s/seed_link_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "seed-link: the control must complete"
assert control.out contains "agreeing_free=yes" else "seed-link: a front door linking only into shipped rooms must pass free"
assert control.out contains "clean_reads_zero=yes" else "seed-link: a clean tree must read zero rather than merely pass"
assert control.out contains "front_dead_refused=yes" else "seed-link: a front-door link into a withheld room must be refused"
assert control.out contains "front_dead_counted=yes" else "seed-link: the refusal must name a count, never only a verdict"
assert control.out contains "front_dead_named=yes" else "seed-link: the refusal must name the document and the link"
assert control.out contains "unshipped_doc_free=yes" else "seed-link: a document the seed never ships cannot break a seed reader's link"
assert control.out contains "ratchet_counted=yes" else "seed-link: a shipped non-front-door link must be counted"
assert control.out contains "ratchet_not_gated=yes" else "seed-link: a ratchet must never be counted against the enforced zero"
assert control.out contains "ratchet_under_ceiling_free=yes" else "seed-link: a ratchet under its ceiling must pass free"
assert control.out contains "dated_testimony_free=yes" else "seed-link: dated testimony keeps every reference it ever wrote"
assert control.out contains "closed_stack_dir_free=yes" else "seed-link: a closed-stack directory (date/, archive/, yonder/) is testimony whatever its basename"
assert control.out contains "mutation_closed_stack_counted=yes" else "seed-link: striking the closed-stack clause must count the page again"
assert control.out contains "external_link_free=yes" else "seed-link: an external or anchor link names no path in this tree"
assert control.out contains "external_not_counted=yes" else "seed-link: an external link must not even be counted as a relative one"
assert control.out contains "ceiling_edge_counted=yes" else "seed-link: the count at the ceiling must be exact"
assert control.out contains "ceiling_edge_free=yes" else "seed-link: a ratchet exactly at its ceiling must pass free"
assert control.out contains "ceiling_over_counted=yes" else "seed-link: the ratchet must count past its ceiling rather than saturate"
assert control.out contains "ceiling_over_refused=yes" else "seed-link: a ratchet over its ceiling must refuse"
assert control.out contains "second_door_refused=yes" else "seed-link: a second-step door linking into a withheld room must be refused"
assert control.out contains "second_door_named=yes" else "seed-link: the refusal must name the second-step door and its link"
assert control.out contains "roster_counted=yes" else "seed-link: the gated roster must report its own size"
assert control.out contains "default_caps_at_five=yes" else "seed-link: the ordinary reading stays short -- five named sites"
assert control.out contains "list_names_every_site=yes" else "seed-link: --list must name every ratchet site, so a lane can find its own share"
assert control.out contains "advice_points_at_list=yes" else "seed-link: a ratchet past the print cap must point a lane at --list"
assert control.out contains "advice_quiet_when_listing=yes" else "seed-link: the advice stays quiet when every site is already named"
assert control.out contains "advice_quiet_under_cap=yes" else "seed-link: the advice stays quiet when the cap names every site anyway"
assert control.out contains "unknown_argument_refused=yes" else "seed-link: an argument the scan does not know must refuse rather than be read past"
assert control.out contains "carried_own_room_uncounted=yes" else "seed-link: a link to the room the projection makes must not be counted"
assert control.out contains "carried_own_room_free=yes" else "seed-link: own-room links past the ceiling must still pass free"
assert control.out contains "carried_ancestor_free=yes" else "seed-link: a link to any room the projection makes must pass free"
assert control.out contains "empty_room_still_counted=yes" else "seed-link: a room no allow row reaches is still a room that is not there"
assert control.out contains "empty_room_named=yes" else "seed-link: the ratchet must name the empty room it counted"
assert control.out contains "mutation_carried_counted=yes" else "seed-link: striking the carried-room clause must count the room again"
assert control.out contains "control_failed=0" else "seed-link: every leg the control runs must read yes"
assert control.out contains "control_legs=33" else "seed-link: a leg added to the control must be heard here on the lap it lands"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "seed-link: the control must agree with itself"
say "RED and GREEN paths proven -- five refusals bitten, one clause struck out of a copy, and every honest reading left free"

say "GREEN: seed-link -- a link in a shipped document lands in the shipped tree."
